> `git diff` only tells you whether a **tracked** file differs from the Git index/HEAD. It does **not** treat ignored/untracked files like `logs/...` as “locally modified.” So for ignored log files:
> 
> 1. local file exists,
> 2. Git says “no tracked diff,”
> 3. script prints:
